# See ENGINEERING_NOTES.md § Snakefile_phase2 (speed-up plan item 5).
#
# collect_viral_positives and annotate_viral_positives were localrules until
# 2026-11-03 and had to be removed: --jobs is a GLOBAL ceiling across every
# executor, not a per-executor one, so once 40 SLURM jobs are queued behind
# the account CPU cap no local job can start at all. Measured on run 1062960:
# 19 samples had all three taxonomy tools finished and zero collect outputs
# existed after 25 h, while stage_sra_paired -- also local -- ran once at the
# start when the queue was still empty. Because run_checkv consumes
# collect's output and annotate consumes CheckV's, the whole tail of the
# pipeline was serialised behind a queue that could not drain. Submitting
# them costs a few seconds of SLURM overhead each and unblocks that chain.
localrules:
    stage_sra_paired, stage_sra_single, stage_local_paired, stage_local_single,
    complete_family_reads, complete_family_downloads

